==Problem 7==

When the World Wide Web first became popular in the <imath>1990</imath>s, download speeds reached a maximum of about <imath>56</imath> kilobits per second. Approximately how many minutes would the download of a <imath>4.2</imath>-megabyte song have taken at that speed? (Note that there are <imath>8000</imath> kilobits in a megabyte.)

<imath>\textbf{(A) } 0.6 \qquad \textbf{(B) } 10 \qquad \textbf{(C) } 1800 \qquad \textbf{(D) } 7200 \qquad \textbf{(E) } 36000</imath>

